# Who owns what, so the two sides of this work stop colliding.
#
# Ruolin authors the TAPP source tables and the composition modules; Stephen authors the schema-path
# placement and everything generated from it. In practice the two have never touched the same file:
# we only ADD *.schemapaths.csv beside his tables, and every one of his files has exactly one commit,
# the import. This makes that split explicit rather than habitual.
#
# CODEOWNERS routes REVIEW; it does not lock files. It only bites with branch protection requiring
# owner approval on pull requests, and it does nothing at all to a direct push. Its real job here is
# to stop our side quietly editing upstream, and to say out loud who answers for what.
#
# ORDER MATTERS: last match wins, and `*` spans dots, so `Module_*.csv` also matches
# `Module_Group1.schemapaths.csv`. The sidecar rules must come AFTER the upstream rules or every
# module sidecar would be owned by the wrong person.

# ---- upstream: authored by Ruolin, imported and never edited on our side --------------------------
/TAPPS*/**/*_TAPP_v*.csv          @ruolin-deng
/TAPPS*/**/Module_*.csv           @ruolin-deng
/TAPPS*/composed_tapps.json       @ruolin-deng
/TAPPS*/README*                   @ruolin-deng

# ---- ours: the placement decisions, and everything generated from them ----------------------------
# These live alongside the upstream tables by design — a sidecar is only meaningful against one
# revision of one table, so it sits next to the table it describes.
/TAPPS*/**/*.schemapaths.csv      @smrTucson
/TAPPS*/**/*.overrides.json       @smrTucson
/_sources/                        @smrTucson
/tools/                           @smrTucson
/docs/                            @smrTucson
/.github/                         @smrTucson

# ---- shared: worth both pairs of eyes ------------------------------------------------------------
/README.md                        @smrTucson @ruolin-deng
/bblocks-config.yaml              @smrTucson @ruolin-deng
